"""Mattermost collaboration platform manifest.

Open-source, self-hosted messaging and collaboration platform for DevSecOps
teams. Single Go binary server with a TypeScript/React web client, PostgreSQL
as the primary store, and a full observability stack (Prometheus, Grafana,
Loki, OTel Collector).

Architecture reference: https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/blob/master/server/docker-compose.yaml
Source: https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost
"""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest
from scryr.types import (
    CalendarVersion,
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    IncrementalVersion,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
    parse_version,
)

_SOURCE = Url("https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost")
_DOCS = Url("https://docs.mattermost.com/")
postgres_block = Manifest(
    name="PostgreSQL",
    icon="🐘",
    classification=Classification.database,
    tags=["database", "sql", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Conversation records\n"
            "\n"
            "Primary relational database storing all Mattermost data: users, teams, channels, posts, preferences, and plugin configurations.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Relational state | Users, channel memberships, and posts |\n"
            "| Recovery scope | Pair database recovery with attachment recovery |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Create a channel and post a message with a test account.\n"
            "2. Restore a test backup and verify membership and post relationships.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** An attachment reference may survive even when its object is unavailable.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *transaction latency, lock waits, and replication or backup age*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - SQL clients for read-only inspection\n"
            "  - Query plans for index review\n"
            "  - Migration tooling for schema changes\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("15.0.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.sql],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.docker_swarm],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
        ],
        links=[Link(site_name="Mattermost Docs", http_url=_DOCS)],
    ),
)
redis_block = Manifest(
    name="Redis",
    icon="🔴",
    classification=Classification.cache_store,
    tags=["cache", "pubsub", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Shared transient state\n"
            "\n"
            "In-memory cache used for session tokens, rate limiting, cluster-wide pub/sub events, and push notification queuing.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Cache entries | Document expiry and invalidation rules |\n"
            "| Events | Distinguish ephemeral notifications from persisted posts |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Expire a test cache entry and observe the application fallback.\n"
            "2. Reconnect a client and compare its history against the database-backed API.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** Lost transient events must not be treated as lost persisted conversations.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *evictions, client connections, and publish or consume failures*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Container logs for process diagnostics\n"
            "  - Resource metrics for capacity review\n"
            "  - Versioned configuration for repeatable environments\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("7.0.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.c],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.docker_swarm],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
