server_block = Manifest(
    name="Mattermost Server",
    icon="💬",
    classification=Classification.internal_api,
    tags=["api", "websocket", "core"],
    connections=[
        Manifest(name="PostgreSQL"),
        Manifest(name="Redis"),
        Manifest(name="MinIO"),
        Manifest(name="Elasticsearch"),
        Manifest(name="OpenLDAP"),
        Manifest(name="Keycloak"),
    ],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Messaging service\n"
            "\n"
            "Core Go application binary exposing the REST API v4, WebSocket event bus, plugin system, workflow automations (Playbooks), Calls voice/video (WebRTC), and the clustering layer for HA deployments.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Request path | Authorize channel access before reading or writing posts |\n"
            "| Event path | Notify connected clients after durable application changes |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Post a message, upload a file, and confirm another client receives the update.\n"
            "2. Disconnect the second client and verify its history after reconnecting.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** A healthy HTTP endpoint does not establish that WebSocket delivery is healthy.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *API latency, active sockets, post errors, and dependency failures*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - `chi`\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Go tooling for builds and tests\n"
            "  - gofmt for source formatting\n"
            "  - Delve for local debugging\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("11.5.1"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.go],
        frameworks=[WebFramework.chi],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.docker_swarm],
        owners="Server",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
        ],
        links=[
            Link(site_name="Mattermost Docs", http_url=_DOCS),
            Link(site_name="API Reference", http_url=Url("https://api.mattermost.com/")),
        ],
    ),
)
